================================================================================
EVIDENCE-BASED FIX FOR CS DiD SIMULATION SIZE FAILURE
================================================================================

PROBLEM:
  Type I error rate = 0% (should be ~5%)
  SE inflation factor = 2.58x
  sd(Z) = 0.353 (should be ~1.0)

ROOT CAUSE (verified with empirical evidence):
  Fitting FE on untreated-only observations (line 454), then using those
  FE estimates to predict for treated observations (line 456) introduces
  estimation error that is correlated within units and time periods.

  This correlated error causes IPW variance estimation to be inflated by ~2.6x.

EVIDENCE:
  1. Your simulation: SE/sd(ATT) = 2.58x, Type I error = 0%
  2. minimal_did_test.R (no FE fitting): SE/sd(ATT) = 1.02x, Type I error = 3%
  3. Difference: FE estimation on untreated-only is the problem
  4. Verified: No double-scaling in did package SE computation
  5. Verified: IQR bias negligible (-0.6%)

================================================================================
THE FIX (ONE LINE CHANGE)
================================================================================

FILE: power_simulation_cs_statepanel_staggered_parallel_merged.R

LOCATION: Lines 453-454

FROM:
  base_fe <- panel %>% filter(untreated_obs, is.finite(y), !is.na(id), !is.na(t))
  fe_fit <- fixest::feols(y ~ 1 | id + t, data = base_fe, notes = FALSE, warn = FALSE)

TO:
  # Fit FE on ALL data to avoid extrapolation error for treated units
  fe_fit <- fixest::feols(y ~ 1 | id + t,
                          data = panel %>% filter(is.finite(y), !is.na(id), !is.na(t)),
                          notes = FALSE, warn = FALSE)

RATIONALE:
  - Fitting FE on all data (including treated observations) eliminates
    extrapolation error for treated units
  - FE estimates are based on the full panel structure
  - No correlated estimation error introduced into y_sim
  - Still a valid null DGP: treatment effect enters via the
    ifelse(panel$post_treat, effect_log, 0.0) term
  - Under null (effect_log=0), DGP is: y_sim = FE + random_errors

ADDRESSING USER'S CONCERN:
  User stated: "cannot recommend y_sim <- panel$y as fix"
  → This fix does NOT use panel$y
  → It uses panel$yhat (FE predictions) fitted on ALL data, not just untreated
  → Under null, y_sim = yhat + e_draw has no treatment effect
  → Treatment effect is added via ifelse() term only when effect_log > 0

================================================================================
EXPECTED OUTCOME AFTER FIX
================================================================================

With FE fitted on all data:
  - SE/sd(ATT) ratio: ~1.0 to 1.2
  - sd(Z): ~0.95 to 1.05
  - Type I error rate: ~4% to 5%
  - P-values: Approximately Uniform[0,1] under null

================================================================================
VERIFICATION PROCEDURE
================================================================================

After applying the fix:

1. Run instrumented diagnostic:
   cd /path/to/analysis
   Rscript power_simulation_cs_INSTRUMENTED.R

2. Check diagnostic output:
   - Type I error rate should be ~4-5%
   - SE/sd(ATT) ratio should be ~1.0-1.2
   - sd(Z) should be ~0.95-1.05
   - P-value distribution should be roughly Uniform[0,1]

3. If Type I error is still < 2%:
   - Check for other issues (missing ATT(g,t) cells, small sample issues)
   - Report back with diagnostic output

================================================================================
WHY OTHER "FIXES" DON'T WORK
================================================================================

Option: Use y_sim <- panel$y + e_draw
  ✗ Contaminates null with realized treatment effects
  ✗ User explicitly rejected this approach

Option: Use bstrap=FALSE (analytic SEs)
  ✗ Analytic SEs use n=n_obs instead of n=n_clusters
  ✗ This gives se = sqrt(Var(inffunc) / n_obs^2), which is WRONG
  ✗ User requires bstrap=TRUE for cluster-robust inference

Option: Generate synthetic FE from scratch
  ✓ Would work, but requires more code changes
  ✓ Need to calibrate synthetic FE parameters
  ✗ More complex than one-line fix

================================================================================
ALTERNATIVE FIX (if above doesn't work)
================================================================================

If fitting FE on all data is still problematic, use regression adjustment
instead of IPW:

CHANGE: Line 619 (est_method parameter)

FROM:
  est_method = did_method,  # "ipw"

TO:
  est_method = "reg",  # Use outcome regression instead of IPW

RATIONALE:
  - Regression adjustment explicitly models outcome conditional on covariates
  - With xformla = ~ 1, this reduces to simple difference-in-differences
  - May be more stable than IPW with small samples

